      "content": "Produce the definitive edit for the task below, using the candidates as drafts.\n\n# Task\nResolve the following GitHub issue in this repository by editing the source code. Do not modify or add tests.\n\n<issue>\nUpdate pyproject.toml to require matplotlib-scalebar > 0.7.0\nThe Matplotlib rcParams Dict doesn't get updated to include scalebar.width_fraction until Release v.0.7.0 of matplotlib-scalebar.\r\n\r\ni.e. version check in ```./pyproject.toml``` should probably change from:\r\n ```matplotlib-scalebar = \">=0.6.2,<0.8.0\"```\r\nto\r\n```matplotlib-scalebar = \">=0.7.0,<0.8.0\"```\n</issue>\n\n# Code (original repository)\n--- AUTHORS.rst ---\n1| ============\n2| Contributors\n3| ============\n4| \n5| * Sarthak Jariwala <jariwala@uw.edu>\n\n--- CONTRIBUTING.rst ---\n1| Contributor Guide\n2| =================\n3| \n4| Thank you for your interest in improving this project.\n5| This project is open-source under the `MIT license`_ and\n6| welcomes contributions in the form of bug reports, feature requests, and pull requests.\n7| \n8| Here is a list of important resources for contributors:\n9| \n10| - `Source Code`_\n11| - `Documentation`_\n12| - `Issue Tracker`_\n13| \n14| .. _MIT license: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\n15| .. _Source Code: https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image\n16| .. _Documentation: https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/\n17| .. _Issue Tracker: https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/issues\n18| \n19| How to report a bug\n20| -------------------\n21| \n22| Report bugs on the `Issue Tracker`_.\n23| \n24| When filing an issue, make sure to answer these questions:\n25| \n26| - Which operating system and Python version are you using?\n27| - Which version of this project are you using?\n28| - What did you do?\n29| - What did you expect to see?\n30| - What did you see instead?\n31| \n32| The best way to get your bug fixed is to provide a test case,\n33| and/or steps to reproduce the issue.\n34| \n35| \n36| How to request a feature\n37| ------------------------\n38| \n39| Request features on the `Issue Tracker`_.\n40| \n41| \n42| How to set up your development environment\n43| ------------------------------------------\n44| \n45| You need Python 3.6+ and the following tools:\n46| \n47| - Poetry_\n48| - Nox_\n49| \n50| Install the package with development requirements:\n51| \n52| .. code:: console\n53| \n54|    $ poetry install\n55| \n56| You can now run an interactive Python session,\n57| or the command-line interface:\n58| \n59| .. code:: console\n60| \n61|    $ poetry run python\n62| \n63| .. _Poetry: https://python-poetry.org/\n64| .. _Nox: https://nox.thea.codes/\n65| \n66| \n67| How to test the project\n68| -----------------------\n69| \n70| Run the full test suite:\n71| \n72| .. code:: console\n73| \n74|    $ nox\n75| \n76| List the available Nox sessions:\n77| \n78| .. code:: console\n79| \n80|    $ nox --list-sessions\n81| \n82| You can also run a specific Nox session.\n83| For example, invoke the unit test suite like this:\n84| \n85| .. code:: console\n86| \n87|    $ nox --session=tests\n88| \n89| Unit tests are located in the ``tests`` directory,\n90| and are written using the pytest_ testing framework.\n91| \n92| .. _pytest: https://pytest.readthedocs.io/\n93| \n94| \n95| How to submit changes\n96| ---------------------\n97| \n98| Open a `pull request`_ to submit changes to this project.\n99| \n100| Your pull request needs to meet the following guidelines for acceptance:\n101| \n102| - The Nox test suite must pass without errors.\n103| - Include unit tests. Code coverage should not decrease.\n104| - If your changes add functionality, update the documentation accordingly.\n105| \n106| Feel free to submit early. We can always iterate on this.\n107| \n108| To run linting and code formatting checks before commiting your change, you can install `pre-commit`_ as a Git hook by running the following command:\n109| \n110| .. code:: console\n111| \n112|    $ pre-commit install\n113| \n114| It is recommended to open an issue before starting work on anything.\n115| This will allow a chance to talk it over and validate your approach.\n116| \n117| .. _pull request: https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/pulls\n118| .. _pre-commit: https://pre-commit.com/\n119| \n120| \n121| Credits\n122| -------\n123| \n124| The above contributing guidelines were adopted from `cookiecutter-hypermodern-python`_ .\n125| \n126| .. _cookiecutter-hypermodern-python: https://github.com/cjolowicz/cookiecutter-hypermodern-python\n\n--- LICENSE.txt ---\n1| The MIT License (MIT)\n2| \n3| Copyright (c) 2020 Sarthak Jariwala\n4| \n5| Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n6| of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n7| in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n8| to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n9| copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n10| furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n11| \n12| The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n13| copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n14| \n15| THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n16| IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n17| FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n18| AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n19| LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n20| OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n21| SOFTWARE.\n\n--- README.md ---\n1| # seaborn-image: image data visualization\n2| \n3| [![Tests](https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/workflows/Tests/badge.svg)](https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/actions?workflow=Tests)\n4| [![Codecov](https://codecov.io/gh/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/branch/master/graph/badge.svg)](https://codecov.io/gh/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image)\n5| [![PyPI](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/seaborn-image.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/seaborn-image/)\n6| [![Documentation Status](https://readthedocs.org/projects/seaborn-image/badge/?version=latest)](https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/?badge=latest)\n7| [![Code style: black](https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-black-000000.svg)](https://github.com/psf/black)\n8| \n9| \n10| <div class=\"row\">\n11| \n12|   <a href=\"https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/plot_image_hist.html\">\n13|   <img src=\"./images/sphx_glr_plot_image_hist_001.png\" height=\"120\" width=\"170\">\n14|   </a>\n15| \n16|   <a href=\"https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/plot_filter.html\">\n17|   <img src=\"./images/sphx_glr_plot_filter_001.png\" height=\"120\" width=\"130\">\n18|   </a>\n19| \n20|   <a href=\"https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/plot_fft.html\">\n21|   <img src=\"./images/sphx_glr_plot_fft_001.png\" height=\"120\" width=\"120\">\n22|   </a>\n23| \n24|   <a href=\"https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/plot_filtergrid.html\">\n25|   <img src=\"./images/sphx_glr_plot_filtergrid_001.png\" height=\"120\" width=\"120\">\n26|   </a>\n27| \n28|   <a href=\"https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/plot_image_robust.html\">\n29|   <img src=\"./images/sphx_glr_plot_image_robust_001.png\" height=\"120\" width=\"260\">\n30|   </a>\n31| \n32| </div>\n33| \n34| \n35| ## Description\n36| \n37| Seaborn-image is a Python **image** visualization library based on matplotlib\n38| and provides a high-level API to **draw attractive and informative images quickly and effectively**.\n39| \n40| It is heavily inspired by [seaborn](https://seaborn.pydata.org/), a high-level visualization library\n41| for drawing attractive statistical graphics in Python.\n42| \n43| ## Documentation\n44| \n45| Detailed documentation can be found [here](https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/).\n46| \n47| - [Tutorial](https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorial.html)\n48| - [Examples](https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/auto_examples/index.html)\n49| - [API Reference](https://seaborn-image.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference.html)\n50| \n51| ## Installation\n52| \n53| For latest release\n54| ```bash\n55| pip install seaborn-image\n56| ```\n57| \n58| For latest commit\n59| ```bash\n60| pip install git+https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image\n61| ```\n62| \n63| ## Contributing\n64| \n65| Please see the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/SarthakJariwala/seaborn-image/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n\n--- data/Perovskite.txt ---\n1| 1371\t1096\t1145\t1107\t1158\t1654\t2183\t2366\t2541\t2696\t2834\t2926\t2507\t1559\t1327\t1574\t1477\t1101\t968\t987\t1177\t1308\t1699\t1540\t1127\t1137\t1299\t1199\t1321\t1283\t1235\t1545\t2591\t3266\t2763\t2337\t2051\t1760\t1669\t1792\t1738\t1531\t1179\t934\t1212\t1345\t1389\t1637\t1845\t1861\n2| 1298\t1099\t1182\t1034\t1380\t2019\t2327\t2287\t2336\t2433\t2550\t2534\t2303\t1507\t1257\t1378\t1216\t999\t1008\t1172\t1179\t1154\t1081\t1035\t1211\t1633\t1697\t1619\t1678\t1539\t1183\t1387\t2302\t2804\t2505\t2118\t1898\t1787\t1780\t1579\t1474\t1234\t939\t865\t1039\t1197\t1252\t1416\t1669\t1749\n3| 1385\t1056\t1173\t1068\t1537\t2112\t2128\t2140\t2086\t2114\t2158\t2076\t1781\t1350\t996\t946\t990\t957\t1013\t1210\t1087\t1086\t892\t924\t1324\t1828\t1860\t1777\t1880\t1834\t1506\t1251\t1491\t1877\t1722\t1605\t1517\t1483\t1500\t1205\t1194\t846\t761\t818\t1024\t1016\t1195\t1264\t1547\t1742\n4| 1386\t1184\t1169\t1062\t1462\t1951\t1913\t1835\t1760\t1687\t1562\t1453\t1448\t1280\t1048\t927\t1066\t1103\t1140\t1158\t1009\t995\t947\t938\t1455\t1858\t1805\t1682\t1655\t1534\t1301\t1039\t1051\t1282\t1171\t1134\t1066\t1051\t913\t914\t854\t800\t831\t937\t1048\t1004\t1079\t1205\t1453\t